From 11bfd4459f1c4ec8b2321175638273a11127e349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:33:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: emulate the depth bounds test in the fragment shader
 biblioklept

There is no hardware depth bounds test. When a pipeline may enable it,
the FS loads the stored depth of each sample with LD_TILE and clears
the SampleMask bit of samples outside [min, max]. The sample index is
kept uniform: LD_TILE returns wrong depths when lanes pass different
indices. The bounds, the enable and the sample count come from graphics
sysvals, so static and dynamic state share one variant. The draw only
declares the depth read while the test is enabled and a depth
attachment is bound. A device-owned FS that only does this test is
bound in place of a missing FS, and only runs while the test is on.
Advertise depthBounds on v10 and v11.

